{
  "comment": "Emax I faceplate, following the panel's own split: PRESET DEFINITION (preset-wide) and ANALOG PROCESSING (per voice). The Emax has no edit buffer: the current preset is edited in RAM, and a voice is addressed by KEY + layer, exactly like the panel's 'Current Voice' (AP 00: Select Lo Voice / Hi Voice, Pri / Sec / Both). 'edit lo' is the key whose voice is read; 'edit lo'..'edit hi' is the range every voice write covers (set lo = A-1, hi = C7 to process the whole keyboard). The layer select is shared across groups (pri / sec / both = one #1A with level 2). Envelopes are AHDSR (not DADSR), so plain knobs rather than the env graph. Edits are heard on the next note, not on held notes. See emax.json driverNotes 2.",
